%description:

RFC 5681 — the initial congestion window is at most the bound of the segment-size table, and
the handshake does not enlarge it.

Checks RFC5681-IW-1 (must, as an upper bound) and RFC5681-IW-2 (must not) from
doc/project/evidence/standard/rfc5681/catalog.md. The English procedure is in
doc/project/evidence/protocol/tcp/checks/congestion-control.md#initial-window; the program
steps below map onto its expected observations. Mapping of the plain mockup: host A = host1,
host B = host2.

This is the first test of the TCP suite that reads a control variable instead of a segment.
The congestion window never travels on the link: it is a limit the sender keeps. The tester
observes it through the `cwnd` scalar signal, which the ini names in `stateSignals`.

The segment size here is 536 bytes, the default of the model and the value RFC 1122 gives
for a host that learns nothing else. 536 falls in the lowest band of the table, so the bound
is 4 * 536 = 2144 bytes.

One property of the model decides what "the initial window" means here. The window is
published only when the algorithm changes it, not when the connection sets it up, so the
first value the signal carries arrives with the first acknowledgment at about t=0.2.

The step says the rule directly: `first()` picks the first publication, and `assertAtMost`
is the bound the table gives. The two halves are separate on purpose. A bound written as a
filter would pick the first publication that is small enough and pass over one that is not,
which is the shape of a check that cannot fail.

The bound governs the initial window alone. After the transfer starts, slow start grows the
window past it, which is what the same section of RFC 5681 requires, and no step here
forbids that.

Expected result: PASS. The bound is an upper bound, so a smaller window conforms.

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

// RFC 5681 §3.1, the lowest band of the table: SMSS <= 1095 gives IW <= 4 * SMSS.
const long SMSS = 536;
const long IW_BOUND = 4 * SMSS;   // 2144 bytes

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("rfc5681_initial_window")
        // Observations 1 and 2 together, in one step. The filter picks the first publication
        // of the window; the assertion is the rule. A model whose first window is too large
        // fails here and the engine does not look for a smaller later one.
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd").first()
                  .assertAtMost(IW_BOUND)
                  .describe("host A's initial congestion window")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "rfc5681_initial_window compiled\n";

%file: test.ned

import inet.node.inet.StandardHost;
import inet.node.ethernet.Eth100M;
import inet.networklayer.configurator.ipv4.Ipv4NetworkConfigurator;

// The plain mockup: host A -- link L -- host B.
network Rfc5681IwNet
{
    submodules:
        configurator: Ipv4NetworkConfigurator { @display("p=100,50"); }
        host1: StandardHost { @display("p=300,100"); }
        host2: StandardHost { @display("p=500,100"); }
    connections:
        host1.ethg++ <--> Eth100M <--> host2.ethg++;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
network = Rfc5681IwNet
sim-time-limit = 2s
seed-set = 0

# Static ARP keeps the wire free of ARP request/reply noise.
**.ipv4.arp.typename = "GlobalArp"

# The congestion window is not a field of a segment, so the tester must be told to observe
# the scalar signal that carries it.
*.protocolTester.stateSignals = "cwnd"

# The segment size of the check. 536 is the lowest band of the table of RFC 5681 §3.1.
**.tcp.mss = 536

# The scenario constants of checks.md#common-mockups. Host B only receives.
*.host1.numApps = 1
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpSessionApp"
*.host1.app[0].connectAddress = "host2"
*.host1.app[0].connectPort = 1000
*.host1.app[0].tOpen = 0.1s
*.host1.app[0].tSend = 0.2s
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 20000B
*.host1.app[0].tClose = 1.5s
*.host2.numApps = 1
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpEchoApp"
*.host2.app[0].localPort = 1000
*.host2.app[0].echoFactor = 0

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST rfc5681_initial_window: PASS
